      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix with the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=-{\\lambda }^{3}-2\\lambda -1.$ Then, ${A}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{3}-2A-I & =O \\\\ {A}^{3} & =-2A-I.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
