    "q-38728": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38728",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6$, find $f(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )+33 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"left\">$\\,\\,{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{2}-3\\,$</td>\n<td colspan=\"7\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"left\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{15}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,5x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,3x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,2x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-2x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{13}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =-2A+6I \\\\  & =-2[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]+6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
